      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tui): coalesce busy submit notices",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users pressing Enter repeatedly while the TUI agent is busy would get a new `agent is busy — press Esc to abort before sending a new message` line appended for every submit attempt, flooding the chat log.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe blocked-submit notice now goes through a shared TUI helper that uses the existing consecutive system-message coalescing behavior. Both the editor-submit path and slash-command busy path use the same helper so repeated blocked submits collapse into one `xN` notice instead of spamming the transcript.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe TUI stays readable when a user accidentally keeps submitting while a run is still active. The user still gets clear feedback and the abort instruction, but repeated attempts increment the existing notice instead of filling the screen.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --parallel-tests \"node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/tui/tui-busy-notice.test.ts src/tui/tui-command-handlers.test.ts\"` — clean, no accepted/actionable findings; focused tests passed.\n- `OPENCLAW_TESTBOX=1 pnpm check:changed` (`blacksmith-testbox`, `tbx_01kwp19xcswyqk4970kcm215yr`).\n- `git diff --check`.\n",
